1
00:00:03,712 --> 00:00:06,089
OKAY...
( gasping )

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,591
NOW, LISTEN, I'M GOING
TO BE MOVING OUT

3
00:00:07,591 --> 00:00:09,844
SO YOU ARE GOING TO BE
IN CHARGE OF PAYING THE RENT.

4
00:00:09,844 --> 00:00:11,846
RIGHT.
AND WHEN IS THAT DUE?

5
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:14,264
FIRST OF THE MONTH.
AND THAT'S EVERY MONTH?

6
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:17,184
NO, JUST THE MONTHS YOU ACTUALLY
WANT TO LIVE HERE.

7
00:00:17,184 --> 00:00:18,560
AH...

8
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,856
OKAY, HERE'S THE PHONE BILL.

9
00:00:21,856 --> 00:00:24,525
OH, MY GOD.

10
00:00:24,525 --> 00:00:27,862
THAT'S OUR PHONE NUMBER.

11
00:00:27,862 --> 00:00:30,029
NOW, LOOK, I KNOW
I KIND OF SPRUNG THIS WHOLE

12
00:00:30,029 --> 00:00:32,533
"ME MOVING OUT ON YOU" THING,
SO WHY DON'T I JUST...

13
00:00:32,533 --> 00:00:33,575
WHY DON'T I JUST COVER
YOU FOR A WHILE?

14
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:34,994
NO, NO, NO WAY.

15
00:00:34,994 --> 00:00:38,956
JOEY TRIBBIANI DOES
NOT TAKE CHARITY...

16
00:00:38,956 --> 00:00:40,749
ANYMORE.

17
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:43,168
IT'S NOT CHARITY, JOE.

18
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:45,462
NO. FORGET IT, OKAY?
I MEAN, THANKS, BUT I'M DONE

19
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:46,964
TAKING MONEY FROM
YOU, ALL RIGHT?

20
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:48,173
I CAN TAKE CARE
OF MYSELF.

21
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:49,717
NOW, WHAT'S
NEXT? COME ON.

22
00:00:49,717 --> 00:00:51,719
OKAY, ALL RIGHT,
HERE'S THE ELECTRIC BILL.

23
00:00:51,719 --> 00:00:53,595
THIS IS HOW MUCH WE
PAY FOR ELECTRIC?!

24
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:54,930
WELL, YEAH.

25
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:56,431
( muttering )

26
00:00:58,726 --> 00:01:02,730
SO WE'LL DO THE REST OF
THE BILLS LATER, THEN?

27
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:13,281
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

28
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:15,492
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

29
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:17,786
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

30
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:22,791
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

31
00:01:22,791 --> 00:01:25,002
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

32
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:27,254
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

33
00:01:27,254 --> 00:01:31,550
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

34
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:37,305
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

35
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:43,478
IS JOEY GOING TO HAVE
TO GIVE UP THE APARTMENT?

36
00:01:43,478 --> 00:01:45,146
WELL, I HOPE NOT.
I TRIED TO OFFER HIM

37
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:46,607
SOME MONEY, BUT HE
WOULDN'T TAKE IT.

38
00:01:46,607 --> 00:01:48,191
WELL, HOW MUCH
DO YOU THINK HE NEEDS?

39
00:01:48,191 --> 00:01:49,693
I FIGURED $1,500
WOULD COVER HIM

40
00:01:49,693 --> 00:01:51,070
FOR A FEW
MONTHS, YOU KNOW?

41
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:53,363
BUT I HAVE TO TRICK
HIM INTO TAKING IT

42
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:54,949
SO I DON'T HURT
HIS PRIDE.

43
00:01:54,949 --> 00:01:57,158
YEAH, WELL, WHY DON'T YOU
HIRE HIM AS AN ACTOR?

44
00:01:57,158 --> 00:01:58,869
YOU COULD HAVE HIM DRESS UP

45
00:01:58,869 --> 00:02:02,456
AND PUT ON LITTLE SKITS--
JUST WHATEVER YOU WANT.

46
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:07,795
WELL, THAT WOULD HELP
THE PRIDE THING.

47
00:02:07,795 --> 00:02:08,796
HEY.

48
00:02:08,796 --> 00:02:10,422
HEY, WOW,
YOU LOOK GREAT.

49
00:02:10,422 --> 00:02:12,633
DO YOU WANT TO MOVE IN
WITH ME TOMORROW?

50
00:02:12,633 --> 00:02:14,301
OKAY.

51
00:02:14,301 --> 00:02:16,553
OKAY. SO, WHAT DO YOU GIRLS

52
00:02:16,553 --> 00:02:17,679
HAVE PLANNED FOR TONIGHT?

53
00:02:17,679 --> 00:02:19,138
WELL, INSTEAD
OF BEING SAD

54
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:20,474
THAT TONIGHT'S MY LAST
THAT NIGHT WITH RACHEL

55
00:02:20,474 --> 00:02:22,517
WE THOUGHT WE'D
GO OUT TO DINNER

56
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:25,270
AND CELEBRATE THE FACT
THAT RACHEL'S MOVING
IN WITH PHOEBE.

57
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:27,397
AND ALSO, MY BIRTHDAY.

58
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:28,607
IT'S NOT YOUR BIRTHDAY.

59
00:02:28,607 --> 00:02:30,442
WHAT A MEAN THING TO SAY.

60
00:02:30,442 --> 00:02:34,154
I WOULD NEVER TELL YOU
IT WAS NOT YOUR BIRTHDAY.

61
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,155
HEY.
HEY.

62
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,448
Phoebe:
HEY.

63
00:02:36,448 --> 00:02:38,325
SO, YOU GUYS HAVE
ANYTHING PLANNED

64
00:02:38,325 --> 00:02:39,994
FOR THE BIG LAST NIGHT?

65
00:02:39,994 --> 00:02:41,787
WELL, INSTEAD
OF JUST HANGING OUT

66
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:43,956
WE FIGURED WE'D DO NOTHING.

67
00:02:43,956 --> 00:02:45,124
WHOA, WHOA,
WHOA, WHOA--

68
00:02:45,124 --> 00:02:47,501
KNICKS SEASON OPENER TONIGHT.

69
00:02:47,501 --> 00:02:50,169
I THOUGHT MAYBE YOU GUYS
WOULD COME OVER AND WATCH IT.

70
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:51,463
I DON'T KNOW, ROSS.

71
00:02:51,463 --> 00:02:52,840
NOT IF YOU'RE
GOING TO TALK ABOUT

72
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,591
HOW YOU GAVE UP
A CAREER IN BASKETBALL

73
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:56,010
TO BECOME A PALEONTOLOGIST.

74
00:02:56,010 --> 00:02:57,845
I DID GIVE UP
A CAREER IN BASKETBALL

75
00:02:57,845 --> 00:02:59,513
TO BECOME A PALEONTOLOGIST.

76
00:02:59,513 --> 00:03:00,681
( groaning )

77
00:03:00,681 --> 00:03:02,891
PHEEBS, I WAS WONDERING...

78
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:04,601
YOU'RE NOT DRESSED YET?

79
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:06,645
WE'RE SUPPOSED TO START
HAVING FUN IN 15 MINUTES.

80
00:03:06,645 --> 00:03:10,691
WELL, AND CLEARLY,
NOT A MINUTE SOONER.

81
00:03:10,691 --> 00:03:13,027
RACHEL, YOU ARE PACKED,
THOUGH, RIGHT?

82
00:03:13,027 --> 00:03:15,029
I MEAN, PLEASE TELL ME
THAT YOU'RE PACKED.

83
00:03:15,029 --> 00:03:16,655
OF COURSE I'M PACKED.

84
00:03:16,655 --> 00:03:18,032
MONICA, RELAX.

85
00:03:18,032 --> 00:03:19,533
I JUST WANTED TO ASK
PHOEBE HER OPINION

86
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:21,076
ON WHAT I SHOULD WEAR TONIGHT.

87
00:03:21,076 --> 00:03:23,829
MY GOD, I CANNOT GET
A MINUTE OF PEACE AROUND HERE.

88
00:03:27,041 --> 00:03:28,500
OH, MY GOD!

89
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,794
YOU'RE NOT PACKED YET.

90
00:03:30,794 --> 00:03:33,630
MONICA'S JUST GOING
TO KILL YOU.

91
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:35,215
YEAH, I-I KNOW.

92
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:37,467
WELL, WHAT YOU'RE WEARING
IS FINE FOR THAT.

93
00:03:39,053 --> 00:03:41,555
RACHEL, I NEED TO TALK...

94
00:03:41,555 --> 00:03:43,098
YOU'RE NOT PACKED!

95
00:03:43,098 --> 00:03:45,559
YOU'RE NOT PACKED
EVEN A LITTLE BIT.

96
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:50,313
SURPRISE!
WHAT?

97
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:51,773
DON'T GET MAD, 'CAUSE, LOOK

98
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:55,234
THIS IS WHAT HAPPENED--
SO I-I STARTED PACKING

99
00:03:55,234 --> 00:03:58,030
AND THEN I REALIZED,
"WHAT AM I DOING?

100
00:03:58,030 --> 00:04:00,115
I AM LOUSY AT
PACKING," RIGHT?

101
00:04:00,115 --> 00:04:02,534
BUT YOU LOVE PACKING

102
00:04:02,534 --> 00:04:06,121
SO AS A GIFT TO YOU
ON OUR LAST NIGHT...

103
00:04:06,121 --> 00:04:09,833
TA-DA.

104
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,960
RIGHT. I'LL BE COORDINATOR.

105
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:14,963
OH, MY GOD, I'M SO SORRY--
I DIDN'T GET YOU ANYTHING.

106
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:17,549
OKAY, LOOK, EVERYBODY
HAS TO HELP, OKAY?

107
00:04:17,549 --> 00:04:19,259
PHOEBE, YOU CAN HELP,
CAN'T YOU?

108
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:20,761
I HAVE PLANS.

109
00:04:20,761 --> 00:04:22,137
YOU HAVE PLANS WITH US.

110
00:04:22,137 --> 00:04:23,680
THAT'S... RIGHT.

111
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:26,349
ALL RIGHT,
CHANDLER CAN MAKE BOXES

112
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:28,393
ROSS CAN WRAP
AND JOEY CAN LIFT THINGS.

113
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:29,853
NOW, PHOEBE, GO TELL THE GUYS
THEY HAVE TO HELP OUT.

114
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:30,938
OKAY.
OKAY.

115
00:04:30,938 --> 00:04:32,689
MY GOD, THANK YOU!

116
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:34,524
HURRY. MONICA'S GOING

117
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:36,401
TO MAKE YOU PACK--
SHE'S GOT JOBS
FOR EVERYONE.

118
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:38,779
NOW, IT'S TOO LATE FOR ME,
BUT SAVE YOURSELVES.

119
00:04:38,779 --> 00:04:42,116
Monica:
OKAY, THE MOVERS
WILL BE HERE

120
00:04:42,116 --> 00:04:43,242
IN 11 HOURS.

121
00:04:43,242 --> 00:04:45,326
RACHEL HAS NOT PACKED.

122
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:46,620
NOW, EVERYBODY HAS TO HELP.

123
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:47,871
CHANDLER, WE'RE GOING
TO START...

124
00:04:47,871 --> 00:04:49,414
NO, I-I-I HAVE PLANS
WITH JOEY.

125
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:50,457
I THOUGHT YOU SAID

126
00:04:50,457 --> 00:04:51,959
YOU WERE GOING TO DO NOTHING.

127
00:04:51,959 --> 00:04:53,835
YES, BUT FOR THE LAST TIME.

128
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:54,836
( sniffling )

129
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:56,504
OKAY, FINE.

130
00:04:56,504 --> 00:04:57,839
NOW, ROSS...

131
00:04:57,839 --> 00:04:59,466
OH, BUT I-I CAN'T DO IT.

132
00:04:59,466 --> 00:05:00,467
WHY NOT?

133
00:05:00,467 --> 00:05:02,052
DON'T YOU HAVE BEN?

134
00:05:02,052 --> 00:05:04,721
BECAUSE...
I HAVE BEN.

135
00:05:04,721 --> 00:05:06,807
IT'S ALMOST 8:00.
IT'S ALMOST PAST HIS BEDTIME.

136
00:05:06,807 --> 00:05:07,808
WHERE IS HE?

137
00:05:07,808 --> 00:05:09,392
HE'S AT A DINNER PARTY.

138
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:14,439
IS HE REALLY COMING? BECAUSE
I CAN SEE INTO YOUR APARTMENT.

139
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:16,191
OF COURSE HE IS.

140
00:05:16,191 --> 00:05:19,653
UH, WHAT, YOU THINK I'D JUST USE
MY SON AS-AS AN EXCUSE?

141
00:05:19,653 --> 00:05:22,405
WHAT KIND OF FATHER
DO YOU THINK I AM?

142
00:05:22,405 --> 00:05:24,158
ALL RIGHT, SORRY.

143
00:05:24,158 --> 00:05:27,077
I GOT TO GO MAKE
A FAKE BEN.

144
00:05:31,248 --> 00:05:33,000
HERE IT IS--

145
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,752
OUR LAST PIZZAS TOGETHER
AS ROOMMATES.

146
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:38,421
I WISH I'D KNOWN YOU
WERE GOING TO DO THAT.
I ORDERED CHINESE.

147
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:40,048
OH, WELL, THAT'S OKAY.

148
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:42,676
HEY, ACTUALLY, IN A WAY,
IT'S KIND OF NICE.

149
00:05:42,676 --> 00:05:44,469
YOU KNOW, OUR LAST
DINNER TOGETHER--

150
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:47,264
ME, BRINGING THE FOOD
OF MY ANCESTORS

151
00:05:47,264 --> 00:05:49,474
YOU, THE FOOD OF YOURS.

152
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:53,103
HUH?

153
00:05:53,103 --> 00:05:54,188
( chuckling )

154
00:05:54,188 --> 00:05:55,605
SAY, JOE, I HAD A STRANGE IDEA

155
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:57,274
FOR WHAT WE COULD DO
FOR OUR LAST NIGHT.

156
00:05:57,274 --> 00:05:59,400
WHAT DO YOU SAY WE PLAY
A LITTLE FOOSBALL FOR MONEY?

157
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,278
ARE YOU CRAZY?

158
00:06:01,278 --> 00:06:04,031
YOU HAVEN'T BEATEN ME ONCE SINCE
MY INJURY-PLAGUED '97 SEASON.

159
00:06:04,031 --> 00:06:06,200
IT'D BE EASIER
IF YOU JUST GIVE ME YOUR MONEY.

160
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,951
YES, IT WOULD.

161
00:06:07,951 --> 00:06:09,286
( clears throat )

162
00:06:09,286 --> 00:06:11,370
WHAT DO YOU SAY TO $50?

163
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:12,580
OKAY, YOU'RE ON.

164
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:13,707
OKAY, LET'S PLAY.

165
00:06:13,707 --> 00:06:15,876
THE BIG GAME--
ITALY VERSUS...

166
00:06:15,876 --> 00:06:17,544
CHINA, APPARENTLY.

167
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,131
OH, LOOK...

168
00:06:21,131 --> 00:06:23,842
IT'S THE ROLLERBLADES.

169
00:06:23,842 --> 00:06:25,302
OH, GOD...

170
00:06:25,302 --> 00:06:28,305
DO YOU REMEMBER
WHEN WE GOT THESE?

171
00:06:28,305 --> 00:06:30,389
NO.

172
00:06:30,389 --> 00:06:33,560
AW, I GUESS YOU WEREN'T THERE.

173
00:06:35,187 --> 00:06:38,273
YOU GUYS, WE SAID WE WERE
GOING TO HAVE FUN.

174
00:06:38,273 --> 00:06:39,274
COME ON, HEY.

175
00:06:39,274 --> 00:06:40,984
REMEMBER THE TIME...?

176
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:42,152
( laughing )

177
00:06:45,947 --> 00:06:48,033
YOU DON'T REMEMBER?

178
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:49,617
I'M SORRY, PHEEBS.

179
00:06:49,617 --> 00:06:52,579
I GUESS I'M JUST REALLY SAD
THAT I'M LEAVING.

180
00:06:52,579 --> 00:06:54,664
I'M GOING TO MISS
YOU SO MUCH.

181
00:06:54,664 --> 00:06:57,251
WELL, THIS DOESN'T HAVE TO BE
SO SAD, THOUGH, YOU KNOW?

182
00:06:57,251 --> 00:06:59,169
MAYBE INSTEAD
OF JUST THINKING ABOUT

183
00:06:59,169 --> 00:07:01,255
HOW MUCH YOU'RE GOING
TO MISS EACH OTHER

184
00:07:01,255 --> 00:07:02,839
YOU SHOULD, LIKE,
THINK ABOUT SOME OF THE THINGS

185
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:06,176
THAT YOU'RE NOT GOING TO MISS.

186
00:07:06,176 --> 00:07:08,762
I DON'T THINK
THERE'S ANYTHING.

187
00:07:08,762 --> 00:07:10,597
COME ON, THERE'S GOT
TO BE SOMETHING.

188
00:07:10,597 --> 00:07:11,848
NOPE.

189
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:13,350
SHE'S PERFECT.

190
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:14,433
HMM.

191
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:18,188
I HAVE ONE.

192
00:07:20,023 --> 00:07:21,816
GREAT. OKAY, YOU CAN GO FIRST.

193
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:24,361
UH, WELL, I GUESS I'M NOT
GOING TO MISS THE FACT...

194
00:07:24,361 --> 00:07:28,573
THAT YOU'RE NEVER ALLOWED
TO MOVE THE PHONE PEN.

195
00:07:32,077 --> 00:07:33,287
GOOD. THAT'S A GOOD ONE.

196
00:07:33,287 --> 00:07:34,746
OKAY, MONICA, ANYTHING?

197
00:07:34,746 --> 00:07:37,332
YOU KNOW, DOES RACHEL MOVE
THE PHONE PEN?

198
00:07:37,332 --> 00:07:40,668
AW, SOMETIMES...

199
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:42,796
ALWAYS, ACTUALLY.

200
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:45,632
OKAY, GOOD. THERE YOU GO.

201
00:07:45,632 --> 00:07:46,967
DOESN'T EVERYONE FEEL BETTER?

202
00:07:46,967 --> 00:07:51,179
IT'S NOT JUST
THE PHONE PEN.

203
00:07:51,179 --> 00:07:53,807
I NEVER GET MY MESSAGES.

204
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:55,558
YOU GET YOUR MESSAGES.

205
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:57,644
YEAH, WELL, I DON'T THINK
IT REALLY COUNTS

206
00:07:57,644 --> 00:07:59,187
IF YOU HAVE TO READ THEM
OFF THE BACK OF YOUR HAND

207
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:02,149
AFTER YOU'VE FALLEN ASLEEP
ON THE COUCH.

208
00:08:02,149 --> 00:08:03,858
SO-SO, YOU MISSED
A MESSAGE FROM WHO?

209
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:06,278
CHANDLER OR YOUR MOM?

210
00:08:06,278 --> 00:08:08,363
OR CHANDLER?

211
00:08:08,363 --> 00:08:10,157
OR YOUR MOM?

212
00:08:14,286 --> 00:08:15,870
GREAT, IT WORKED.
NO ONE'S SAD.

213
00:08:18,623 --> 00:08:19,874
YES.
( groaning )

214
00:08:19,874 --> 00:08:21,335
I WIN AGAIN.

215
00:08:21,335 --> 00:08:23,337
HA-HA, THAT'S, LIKE,
500 BUCKS YOU OWE ME.

216
00:08:23,337 --> 00:08:24,338
WHOO-HOO-HOO.

217
00:08:24,338 --> 00:08:26,673
YEAH. $500...

218
00:08:26,673 --> 00:08:29,384
THAT IS A LOT OF ELECTRICITY,
HUH?

219
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:30,927
WHOO-HOO-HOO.

220
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:33,763
OOH, I GOT TO BUY SOME FOOD.

221
00:08:33,763 --> 00:08:35,974
OKAY, OKAY, GIVE ME A CHANCE
TO WIN MY MONEY BACK, OKAY?

222
00:08:35,974 --> 00:08:37,934
SUDDEN DEATH, ONE GOAL...

223
00:08:37,934 --> 00:08:39,769
$1,000.

224
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:40,770
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

225
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:41,896
OH, YES.

226
00:08:41,896 --> 00:08:43,273
OKAY...

227
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:44,691
GET READY TO OWE ME.

228
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:45,859
OKAY.

229
00:08:45,859 --> 00:08:47,068
OKAY, HERE WE GO. READY?

230
00:09:11,510 --> 00:09:13,594
NO, NO, NO.
NO, NO, NO.

231
00:09:13,594 --> 00:09:18,016
NO.... ONE CAN BEAT ME.
( groaning )

232
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:21,728
SEE? NOW, THAT'S WHY

233
00:09:21,728 --> 00:09:24,647
ONLY THE LITTLE FAKE MEN
ARE SUPPOSED TO DO THE KICKING.

234
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:29,236
( phone ringing )

235
00:09:29,236 --> 00:09:30,362
HELLO?

236
00:09:30,362 --> 00:09:31,946
OH, HI, ROSS.

237
00:09:31,946 --> 00:09:33,740
SEE? OTHER PEOPLE CALL ME.

238
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:36,617
OOH, YOUR BROTHER-- SCORE.

239
00:09:37,618 --> 00:09:39,454
WHAT'S UP?

240
00:09:39,454 --> 00:09:40,997
Oh, I'm just over here with Ben.

241
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,832
THOUGHT WE'D SAY HI.

242
00:09:42,832 --> 00:09:43,875
OH, PUT HIM ON.

243
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:46,878
BEN, SAY HI TO AUNT MONICA.

244
00:09:46,878 --> 00:09:51,341
OH, I GUESS HE DOESN'T FEEL
LIKE TALKING RIGHT NOW.

245
00:09:51,341 --> 00:09:54,261
UH, HE'S SMILING, THOUGH.

246
00:09:54,261 --> 00:09:57,889
OKAY, TALK TO YOU LATER.

247
00:10:04,521 --> 00:10:07,023
I THINK IT WAS BETTER
WHEN YOU GUYS WERE SAD.

248
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:08,442
HEY, OH...

249
00:10:08,442 --> 00:10:09,650
REMEMBER THE ROLLERBLADES?

250
00:10:09,650 --> 00:10:12,237
( sobbing ):
OH...

251
00:10:12,237 --> 00:10:14,239
YOU KNOW WHAT ELSE
I'M NOT GOING TO MISS?

252
00:10:14,239 --> 00:10:17,158
"I'M MONICA. I WASH THE TOILET
17 TIMES A DAY

253
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:20,245
EVEN IF PEOPLE ARE ON IT."

254
00:10:20,245 --> 00:10:22,497
"HI, I'M RACHEL.
IS MY SWEATER TOO TIGHT?

255
00:10:22,497 --> 00:10:25,959
NO? OH, I BETTER WASH IT
AND SHRINK IT."

256
00:10:25,959 --> 00:10:27,752
"I'M MONICA.

257
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:29,963
I DON'T GET PHONE MESSAGES
FROM INTERESTING PEOPLE. EVER."

258
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:31,214
HEY, I CALL HER.

259
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:35,676
"OH, MY GOD, I LOVE ROSS,
I HATE ROSS.

260
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:38,721
I LOVE ROSS, I HATE ROSS."

261
00:10:38,721 --> 00:10:40,723
"OH, MY GOD,
I CAN'T FIND A BOYFRIEND

262
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:42,976
"SO I GUESS I'LL JUST
STUMBLE ACROSS THE HALL

263
00:10:42,976 --> 00:10:45,604
AND SLEEP WITH THE FIRST GUY
I FIND IN THERE."

264
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:52,402
YEAH, WE SHOULD
GET A MOVE ON

265
00:10:52,402 --> 00:10:55,447
IF WE WANT TO MAKE
THOSE DINNER RESERVATIONS.

266
00:11:01,995 --> 00:11:04,331
STILL BROKEN?

267
00:11:04,331 --> 00:11:06,040
IT SUCKS, MAN.

268
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,375
IT'S YOUR LAST NIGHT HERE
AND I LOSE THE TWO MOST

269
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:09,085
IMPORTANT THINGS IN MY LIFE--

270
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:11,505
THE FOOSBALL TABLE AND...

271
00:11:11,505 --> 00:11:14,048
$500.

272
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:15,133
BUT, YOU KNOW,
THERE ARE OTHER WAYS

273
00:11:15,133 --> 00:11:16,468
YOU CAN WIN BACK YOUR MONEY.

274
00:11:16,468 --> 00:11:18,345
HOW ABOUT A LITTLE,
UH, A LITTLE BLACKJACK?

275
00:11:18,345 --> 00:11:19,638
NAH, NOT MY GAME.

276
00:11:19,638 --> 00:11:21,306
OKAY, UH, HOW ABOUT--
HOW ABOUT...

277
00:11:21,306 --> 00:11:22,807
YOU KNOW, WE COULD
PLAY A NEW GAME.

278
00:11:22,807 --> 00:11:24,142
A NEW GAME-- IT'S FUN.

279
00:11:24,142 --> 00:11:25,310
WELL, WHAT'S IT CALLED?

280
00:11:26,645 --> 00:11:28,647
CUPS.

281
00:11:28,647 --> 00:11:30,273
I DON'T KNOW HOW TO PLAY CUPS.

282
00:11:30,273 --> 00:11:31,732
I'LL TEACH
YOU. COME ON.

283
00:11:31,732 --> 00:11:33,276
IT'S REAL EASY...
REALLY, REALLY FUN.

284
00:11:33,276 --> 00:11:36,695
ALL RIGHT.
OKAY, HERE YOU GO.

285
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:37,780
I HAVE TWO QUEENS.

286
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,865
WHAT DO YOU HAVE?

287
00:11:38,865 --> 00:11:40,158
A TWO AND A FIVE.

288
00:11:40,158 --> 00:11:41,535
HO-HO, YOU WIN, $50.

289
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:44,787
REALLY?

290
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:46,289
OH, YEAH. OKAY,
LET'S PLAY AGAIN.

291
00:11:46,289 --> 00:11:47,332
READY?

292
00:11:47,332 --> 00:11:48,625
( chuckling )

293
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:50,502
WHAT HAVE YOU GOT?

294
00:11:50,502 --> 00:11:52,379
FOUR AND A NINE.

295
00:11:52,379 --> 00:11:54,548
YOU'RE KIDDING, RIGHT?

296
00:11:54,548 --> 00:11:56,341
NO. WHY?

297
00:11:56,341 --> 00:11:58,385
WELL, THAT'S A FULL CUP.

298
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,680
DAMN, I AM GOOD AT CUPS.

299
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:06,351
I'M NOT TALKING TO HER.

300
00:12:06,351 --> 00:12:08,144
ONE OF YOU HAS
TO TAKE THE FIRST STEP

301
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:09,479
AND IT SHOULD BE YOU

302
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:10,689
BECAUSE SHE'S THE ONE
WHO'S LEAVING.

303
00:12:10,689 --> 00:12:12,106
IT'S HARDER FOR HER.

304
00:12:13,483 --> 00:12:15,276
WELL, MAYBE
YOU'RE RIGHT...

305
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,987
BUT SHE MADE FUN
OF MY PHONE PEN!

306
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:18,988
I KNOW.

307
00:12:18,988 --> 00:12:20,907
I TOOK IT HARD, TOO.

308
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:27,080
LISTEN, RACHEL, I FEEL
REALLY BAD ABOUT WHAT HA...

309
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,498
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

310
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:29,748
I'M UNPACKING.

311
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:31,918
WHAT?!
I'M NOT MOVING.

312
00:12:31,918 --> 00:12:33,836
IS THAT PICTURE STRAIGHT?

313
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:36,881
IT NEEDS TO GO
ABOUT 20 BLOCKS TO THE LEFT.

314
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:38,883
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT--
YOU'RE THE ONE WHO WANTS

315
00:12:38,883 --> 00:12:41,010
TO MAKE THIS BIG CHANGE
AND MOVE IN WITH CHANDLER.

316
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:43,346
YOU SHOULD BE THE ONE TO GO;
WHY DO I HAVE TO LEAVE?

317
00:12:43,346 --> 00:12:44,556
BECAUSE IT'S MY APARTMENT.

318
00:12:44,556 --> 00:12:46,015
WELL, IT'S MINE, TOO.

319
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:47,267
WHAT ELSE YOU GOT?

320
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:50,144
HOW ABOUT... YOU'RE MOVING?!

321
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:52,355
WH...
NO. NO-NO-NO.

322
00:12:52,355 --> 00:12:53,648
YES, YES,
YES-YES-YES.
NO-NO-NO-NO.

323
00:12:53,648 --> 00:12:55,442
YES.
NO-NO-NO.

324
00:12:55,442 --> 00:12:56,443
YES.
NO-NO-NO.

325
00:12:56,443 --> 00:12:57,944
OKAY, MONICA, WAIT!

326
00:12:57,944 --> 00:12:58,945
COME ON.

327
00:12:58,945 --> 00:12:59,946
COME ON.

328
00:12:59,946 --> 00:13:02,282
THIS IS RIDICULOUS.

329
00:13:04,117 --> 00:13:05,326
WE SHOULD BE
PACKING YOU!

330
00:13:05,326 --> 00:13:06,785
WH...

331
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:08,955
Phoebe:
HEY, HOW YOU GUYS DOING?

332
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:11,750
GREAT.
MONICA'S MOVING.

333
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:13,334
I AM NOT.

334
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:17,088
OH, REALLY? WELL, HOW COME
ALL YOUR STUFF IS IN THIS BOX?

335
00:13:17,088 --> 00:13:18,632
OKAY, YOU GUYS, YOU GUYS

336
00:13:18,632 --> 00:13:21,008
I THINK I KNOW WHAT'S
GOING ON, HERE, OKAY?

337
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:23,344
YOU GUYS... STOP!

338
00:13:23,344 --> 00:13:25,764
I KNOW THAT... I KNOW
THAT YOU'RE ACTING MAD

339
00:13:25,764 --> 00:13:28,475
BECAUSE YOU THINK
THAT'LL MAKE IT EASIER TO LEAVE

340
00:13:28,475 --> 00:13:30,435
BUT DEEP DOWN,
YOU'RE STILL REALLY SAD--

341
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:31,436
DEEP, DEEP DOWN.

342
00:13:31,436 --> 00:13:33,438
NO, PHOEBE, I AM MAD.

343
00:13:33,438 --> 00:13:35,814
WELL, DEEP,
DEEP, DEEP DOWN.
YEAH, I'M JUST MAD.

344
00:13:35,814 --> 00:13:37,734
THEN, KEEP RUNNING.

345
00:13:40,612 --> 00:13:42,280
YOU WIN.

346
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:44,073
WELL, WHAT DID YOU HAVE?
WELL, IT DOESN'T MATTER.

347
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:47,619
NOTHING BEATS A...
THREE AND A SIX.

348
00:13:47,619 --> 00:13:49,870
THAT, MY FRIEND,
IS "D" CUP.

349
00:13:51,665 --> 00:13:54,501
OKAY, NOW, HOW MUCH
HAVE YOU WON SO FAR?

350
00:13:54,501 --> 00:13:55,710
UH... WOW...

351
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:56,711
$700.

352
00:13:56,711 --> 00:13:58,171
NOT $700 EXACTLY?

353
00:13:58,171 --> 00:13:59,339
YEAH.

354
00:13:59,339 --> 00:14:00,757
DOUBLE IT.

355
00:14:00,757 --> 00:14:02,216
WHAT?

356
00:14:02,216 --> 00:14:03,635
YEAH, SEE, IN CUPS

357
00:14:03,635 --> 00:14:06,262
ONCE YOU GET $700,
YOU HAVE TO DOUBLE IT.

358
00:14:06,262 --> 00:14:07,806
REALLY?

359
00:14:07,806 --> 00:14:10,016
HEY, I DIDN'T
MAKE UP THE RULES.

360
00:14:10,016 --> 00:14:11,892
OKAY, SO, NOW

361
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:14,354
AFTER YOU RECEIVE
THE DOUBLING BONUS

362
00:14:14,354 --> 00:14:15,938
YOU GET, UH, ONE CARD.

363
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:18,566
NOW, THAT ONE CARD
COULD BE WORTH $100

364
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:20,943
WHICH BRINGS YOUR
TOTAL TO $1,500.

365
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:21,944
OH-HO...
NO, WAIT.

366
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:23,363
DON'T GET TOO EXCITED

367
00:14:23,363 --> 00:14:25,198
BECAUSE THAT'S NOT
GOING TO HAPPEN

368
00:14:25,198 --> 00:14:26,825
UNLESS YOU GET
THE... NO WAY!

369
00:14:29,494 --> 00:14:31,788
WELL, THIS IS THE LAST
BOX OF YOUR CLOTHES.

370
00:14:31,788 --> 00:14:33,206
I'M JUST GOING
TO LABEL IT

371
00:14:33,206 --> 00:14:35,124
"WHAT WERE YOU THINKING?"

372
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:36,668
HUH, THAT'S SO FUNNY

373
00:14:36,668 --> 00:14:38,712
'CAUSE I WAS JUST GOING TO GO
ACROSS THE HALL

374
00:14:38,712 --> 00:14:40,213
AND WRITE THAT ON CHANDLER.

375
00:14:42,716 --> 00:14:45,009
OKAY, YOU GUYS, I DON'T MEAN
TO MAKE THINGS WORSE

376
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:47,679
BUT, UM, I DON'T WANT TO LIVE
WITH RACHEL ANYMORE.

377
00:14:47,679 --> 00:14:49,055
WHAT?
WHAT?

378
00:14:49,055 --> 00:14:50,931
YOU'RE JUST SO
MEAN TO EACH OTHER

379
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:52,642
AND I DON'T WANT
TO END UP LIKE THAT WITH RACHEL.

380
00:14:52,642 --> 00:14:54,435
I STILL LIKE YOU.

381
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:57,397
WELL, PHOEBE, THAT'S FINE
BECAUSE I'M NOT MOVING.

382
00:14:57,397 --> 00:14:59,065
WHOA-WHOA-WHOA-WHOA-WHOA.

383
00:14:59,065 --> 00:15:01,568
PHOEBE, YOU GOT TO TAKE HER.

384
00:15:01,568 --> 00:15:03,444
I KNOW I SAID
SOME BAD STUFF ABOUT HER

385
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:05,405
BUT RACHEL DOES HAVE
SOME GOOD QUALITIES

386
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:06,781
THAT MAKE HER
A GOOD ROOMMATE.

387
00:15:06,781 --> 00:15:09,617
OH, REALLY?
LIKE WHAT, MONICA?

388
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:10,910
OKAY...

389
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:13,913
YOU KNOW HOW SHE HAS
147,000 PAIR OF BOOTS?

390
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:15,874
OH, YEAH, GOOD START, MON.

391
00:15:15,874 --> 00:15:17,876
SHE LETS YOU BORROW THEM.

392
00:15:17,876 --> 00:15:21,920
YEAH, AND YOU STRETCH THEM OUT
WITH YOUR BIG OLD CLOWN FEET.

393
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,090
DO YOU WANT TO LIVE OUTSIDE?

394
00:15:24,090 --> 00:15:26,259
BECAUSE IT'S GETTING COLD.

395
00:15:27,844 --> 00:15:29,220
SHE GETS TONS OF CATALOGS

396
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:30,680
AND, UM,
SHE'LL FOLD DOWN THE PAGES

397
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:33,099
OF THE THINGS
THAT SHE THINKS THAT I'D LIKE.

398
00:15:33,099 --> 00:15:34,517
WHAT ELSE?

399
00:15:34,517 --> 00:15:35,685
WELL...

400
00:15:35,685 --> 00:15:37,437
WHEN I TAKE A SHOWER...

401
00:15:37,437 --> 00:15:40,565
SHE LEAVES ME LITTLE NOTES
ON THE MIRROR.

402
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:41,566
YEAH, I DO.

403
00:15:41,566 --> 00:15:42,942
I-I DO DO THAT.

404
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,444
THAT'S NICE.

405
00:15:44,444 --> 00:15:47,154
I LIKE HAVING THINGS TO READ
IN THE BATHROOM.

406
00:15:48,865 --> 00:15:50,283
WHEN I FALL ASLEEP

407
00:15:50,283 --> 00:15:51,910
ON THE COUCH
AFTER READING...

408
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:55,121
SHE COVERS ME OVER
WITH A BLANKET.

409
00:15:55,121 --> 00:15:56,790
WELL, YOU KNOW...

410
00:15:56,790 --> 00:15:59,125
I DON'T WANT YOU TO BE COLD.

411
00:16:00,627 --> 00:16:03,254
( voice breaking ):
AND... WHEN I TOLD HER

412
00:16:03,254 --> 00:16:06,591
THAT I WAS GOING TO BE MOVING IN
WITH CHANDLER...

413
00:16:06,591 --> 00:16:08,384
SHE WAS REALLY SUPPORTIVE.

414
00:16:11,011 --> 00:16:13,973
( crying ):
YOU WERE SO GREAT.

415
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:16,726
YOU MADE IT
SO EASY...

416
00:16:18,185 --> 00:16:20,939
AND, NOW YOU
HAVE TO LEAVE...

417
00:16:20,939 --> 00:16:22,607
AND I HAVE TO
LIVE WITH A BOY!

418
00:16:22,607 --> 00:16:23,608
OH...

419
00:16:23,608 --> 00:16:24,609
OH, HONEY...

420
00:16:24,609 --> 00:16:26,277
( crying )

421
00:16:26,277 --> 00:16:29,489
OH, IT'S GOING TO BE FINE.

422
00:16:29,489 --> 00:16:32,450
OKAY, RACHEL, NOW I CAN'T
WAIT TO LIVE WITH YOU...

423
00:16:32,450 --> 00:16:34,285
AND YOU KNOW WHAT
WE SHOULD DO?

424
00:16:34,285 --> 00:16:36,579
BRING MONICA, AND, THEN
WE COULD ALL LIVE THERE TOGETHER

425
00:16:36,579 --> 00:16:38,581
AND WE'LL HAVE SO MUCH FUN!

426
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:42,335
BUT, HONEY, I THINK SHE'S
MOVING IN WITH CHANDLER.

427
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:43,962
OH, THAT'S RIGHT.

428
00:16:43,962 --> 00:16:45,672
YOU'RE STILL SET ON THAT?

429
00:16:45,672 --> 00:16:46,673
( sniffles )

430
00:16:46,673 --> 00:16:48,090
KIND OF.

431
00:16:54,806 --> 00:16:56,140
OH, MY GOD!

432
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:59,477
( phone rings )

433
00:16:59,477 --> 00:17:00,478
HELLO?

434
00:17:00,478 --> 00:17:01,479
HEY, MON.

435
00:17:01,479 --> 00:17:03,063
HOW'S THE PACKING GOING?

436
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:04,022
BEN? HE'S FINE.

437
00:17:04,022 --> 00:17:05,316
YEAH, HE'S RIGHT...

438
00:17:05,316 --> 00:17:07,234
OH, MY GOD!

439
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:08,736
WELL...

440
00:17:08,736 --> 00:17:11,197
GET YOUR HEAD OUT OF
YOUR SHIRT THERE, SON.

441
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:12,532
( chuckles nervously )

442
00:17:12,532 --> 00:17:13,867
WHAT?

443
00:17:13,867 --> 00:17:15,284
YEAH, IT'S A PUMPKIN.

444
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:16,452
I'LL COME PACK.

445
00:17:19,706 --> 00:17:21,040
HEY.

446
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,166
WHAT'S WRONG?

447
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:23,167
ROSS AND I

448
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:24,460
WERE HELPING THE GIRLS PACK

449
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,503
TOOK A LITTLE BREAK...

450
00:17:25,503 --> 00:17:29,048
I LOST $1,500 TO HIM AT CUPS.

451
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,049
WHA...

452
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:33,052
HOW DID YOU LOSE AT CUPS?

453
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,554
THE SAME WAY YOU LOST.

454
00:17:34,554 --> 00:17:37,056
I STARTED OUT WITH
A KING AND A QUEEN.

455
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:39,308
BAM! ROSS GETS A
TWO AND A THREE.

456
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:41,227
THEN I GET A JACK AND A KING.

457
00:17:41,227 --> 00:17:43,270
BOOM! ROSS GETS A FOUR AND FIVE.

458
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,732
ROSS WAS GETTING
THE CUP CARD

459
00:17:45,732 --> 00:17:48,902
TH-THE "D" CUP,
THE-THE SITTING-DOWN BONUS...

460
00:17:48,902 --> 00:17:52,613
MEANWHILE, I DIDN'T EVEN GET
A HALF A CUP, NOTHING!

461
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:54,574
OH, MAN!

462
00:17:54,574 --> 00:17:56,951
HE NEVER PLAYED BEFORE EITHER.
YOU KNOW WHAT I THINK?

463
00:17:56,951 --> 00:18:00,329
I THINK BEGINNER'S LUCK--
VERY IMPORTANT IN CUPS.

464
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:01,831
OKAY, I...
LET'S JUST PLAY ONE MORE HAND--

465
00:18:01,831 --> 00:18:03,416
JUST ONE MORE HAND.

466
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:05,960
NO, NO, NO MORE--
I CANNOT LOSE ANOTHER DIME.

467
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,503
I'M SERIOUS THIS TIME.

468
00:18:07,503 --> 00:18:09,047
I-IN FACT, LOOK, THERE'S, UH...

469
00:18:09,047 --> 00:18:10,840
I WANT TO GIVE
YOU SOMETHING, OKAY?

470
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:14,301
AND LET ME GIVE IT TO YOU NOW,
BEFORE I PAWN IT FOR CUPS MONEY.

471
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:18,598
NOW... I WANT YOU TO HAVE

472
00:18:18,598 --> 00:18:21,642
THE BIG WHITE DOG
AS A... KIND OF A, YOU KNOW

473
00:18:21,642 --> 00:18:25,229
LIKE A THANK YOU FOR...
BEING SUCH A GREAT ROOMMATE.

474
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:27,648
I CAN'T TAKE THE
BIG WHITE DOG.

475
00:18:27,648 --> 00:18:28,816
YOU LOVE IT.

476
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:31,611
IT'S "HIM," NOT "IT."

477
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:33,111
NO, BUT WHAT-WHAT
IF I BOUGHT IT

478
00:18:33,111 --> 00:18:34,614
FROM YOU, YOU KNOW?

479
00:18:34,614 --> 00:18:36,741
AND, THEN, YOUR-YOUR
NICE GESTURE WOULD BE

480
00:18:36,741 --> 00:18:38,743
GIVING IT TO ME
AT A REASONABLE PRICE--

481
00:18:38,743 --> 00:18:40,369
( voice cracking ):
SAY, $1,500?

482
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:43,121
WAIT A SECOND.

483
00:18:43,121 --> 00:18:45,083
I SEE WHAT YOU'RE TRYING
TO DO HERE.

484
00:18:45,083 --> 00:18:48,377
YOU'RE-YOU'RE-YOU'RE TRYING
TO GIVE ME MONEY AGAIN.

485
00:18:48,377 --> 00:18:50,546
WHEN DID I TRY
TO GIVE YOU MONEY?

486
00:18:50,546 --> 00:18:52,423
BEFORE, OVER THERE,
WITH THE BILLS.

487
00:18:52,423 --> 00:18:53,549
YOU TRIED TO GIVE ME CHARITY.

488
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:55,927
I SAID, "NO."
YOU DROPPED IT.

489
00:18:55,927 --> 00:18:57,720
OKAY, THEN, WE HAD
A NICE LAST NIGHT TOGETHER.

490
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:59,639
WE HAD SOME FUN; WE GAMBLED.

491
00:18:59,639 --> 00:19:01,557
NOBODY TRIED
TO GIVE ANYBODY ANY MONEY.

492
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:06,687
NOW, OUT OF THE BLUE, YOU START
WITH THE CHARITY THING AGAIN.

493
00:19:06,687 --> 00:19:08,689
I'M JUST TRYING
TO HELP YOU OUT, OKAY?

494
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:10,441
I WANT TO MAKE SURE
THAT YOU'RE OKAY.

495
00:19:10,441 --> 00:19:12,068
I WILL BE OKAY.

496
00:19:12,068 --> 00:19:14,862
LOOK, CHANDLER, YOU GOT
TO GET IT OUT OF YOUR HEAD

497
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:17,073
THAT I CAN'T TAKE CARE
OF MYSELF, OKAY?

498
00:19:17,073 --> 00:19:18,616
LOOK, I'M NOT GOING

499
00:19:18,616 --> 00:19:21,368
TO MISS YOU HELPING ME OUT
WITH MONEY.

500
00:19:21,368 --> 00:19:24,204
THE ONLY THING
THAT I'M GOING TO MISS...

501
00:19:24,204 --> 00:19:26,206
IS YOU...

502
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:30,711
AND, NOW THE DOG.

503
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:39,012
HEY...

504
00:19:39,012 --> 00:19:40,262
CALL ME WHEN YOU
GET THERE, OKAY?

505
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:41,514
OKAY.

506
00:19:41,514 --> 00:19:43,474
I'M REALLY GOING
TO MISS YOU.

507
00:19:43,474 --> 00:19:45,143
MMM.

508
00:19:45,143 --> 00:19:47,061
( both sigh )

509
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,732
OH, I HAVE YOUR KEY.

510
00:19:53,026 --> 00:19:54,360
HERE YOU GO.

511
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:55,361
THANKS.

512
00:19:55,361 --> 00:19:56,529
OKAY.

513
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,576
OH, GOD, THIS IS SILLY.

514
00:20:02,576 --> 00:20:05,038
I'M GOING TO SEE YOU
IN A COUPLE OF HOURS.

515
00:20:05,038 --> 00:20:06,706
MM-HMM.

516
00:20:06,706 --> 00:20:08,541
BYE, HOUSE.

517
00:20:08,541 --> 00:20:09,876
( chuckling )

518
00:20:13,253 --> 00:20:15,089
BYE, BABE.
BYE.

519
00:20:37,904 --> 00:20:40,239
HI.

520
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:41,908
SHE REALLY LEFT.

521
00:20:41,908 --> 00:20:43,492
I KNOW.

522
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:46,996
THANK YOU.

523
00:20:46,996 --> 00:20:48,831
NO PROBLEM, ROOMIE.

524
00:20:56,839 --> 00:20:58,549
CAN I ASK YOU A QUESTION?

525
00:20:58,549 --> 00:20:59,884
SURE.

526
00:20:59,884 --> 00:21:02,887
WHAT THE HELL IS
THAT DOG DOING HERE?

527
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:10,394
I INVENTED CUPS
AS A WAY TO
GIVE JOEY MONEY.

528
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:12,438
AND, NOW YOU WANT
THAT MONEY BACK.

529
00:21:12,438 --> 00:21:14,023
EXACTLY.

530
00:21:14,023 --> 00:21:16,609
CHANDLER, WHAT KIND OF IDIOT
DO YOU TAKE ME FOR?

531
00:21:16,609 --> 00:21:18,277
IT'S NOT A REAL GAME.

532
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:20,196
I MADE IT UP.

533
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:23,323
I'M SORRY YOU LOST YOUR MONEY,
BUT I WON IT FAIR AND SQUARE.

534
00:21:23,323 --> 00:21:25,243
AT A FAKE GAME!

535
00:21:25,243 --> 00:21:29,247
NOW, IF YOU WANT TO TRY
TO MAKE SOME OF IT BACK...

536
00:21:29,247 --> 00:21:32,041
I'D BE GLAD TO PLAY YOU FOR IT,
BUT I SHOULD WARN YOU--

537
00:21:32,041 --> 00:21:35,795
I AM VERY GOOD AT CUPS.

538
00:21:35,795 --> 00:21:37,004
OKAY...

539
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:39,006
NOW, I ASSUME
THE SAUCER CARD CAME UP

540
00:21:39,006 --> 00:21:40,258
WHEN YOU PLAYED LAST.

541
00:21:40,258 --> 00:21:42,551
NO.
HMM...

542
00:21:42,551 --> 00:21:44,678
LET'S SEE IF IT COMES UP
THIS TIME.

